tk-verified-tags: TPMT_TK_VERIFIED accepts the version 185 ticket tags

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix (pre-185 behavior).

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 2, version 185, Table "Definition of
TPMT_TK_VERIFIED Structure"): "#TPM_RC_TAG | | error returned when *tag* is
not one of the values in @tbl:tpm-st-for-signatures", where that table lists
`TPM_ST_VERIFIED`, `TPM_ST_MESSAGE_VERIFIED` and `TPM_ST_DIGEST_VERIFIED`;
Table "Definition of TPMU_TK_VERIFIED_META Union": "digestVerified |
TPMI_ALG_HASH | `TPM_ST_DIGEST_VERIFIED`".

The reference (written before version 185) accepts only TPM_ST_VERIFIED and
returns TPM_RC_TAG for the other two tags, which version 185 (and tpm-rs)
unmarshal, with the TPMI_ALG_HASH metadata of TPM_ST_DIGEST_VERIFIED. The patch
accepts both tags and unmarshals (and discards) that metadata. A ticket with
these tags cannot be valid on this TPM (it implements neither
TPM2_VerifySequenceComplete nor TPM2_VerifyDigestSignature), so
TPM2_PolicyAuthorize still rejects it when it compares the ticket.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/support/Marshal.c
@@ -1922,11 +1922,23 @@
 {
     TPM_RC result;
     result = TPM_ST_Unmarshal((TPM_ST*)&(target->tag), buffer, size);
-    if((result == TPM_RC_SUCCESS) && (target->tag != TPM_ST_VERIFIED))
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // version 185 adds TPM_ST_MESSAGE_VERIFIED (0x8026) and
+    // TPM_ST_DIGEST_VERIFIED (0x8027, with a TPMI_ALG_HASH metadata field) to
+    // the tags of TPMT_TK_VERIFIED (Part 2, TPMT_TK_VERIFIED and
+    // TPMU_TK_VERIFIED_META); the metadata is not kept (no such ticket can be
+    // valid here).
+    if((result == TPM_RC_SUCCESS) && (target->tag != TPM_ST_VERIFIED)
+       && (target->tag != 0x8026) && (target->tag != 0x8027))
         result = TPM_RC_TAG;
     if(result == TPM_RC_SUCCESS)
         result = TPMI_RH_HIERARCHY_Unmarshal(
             (TPMI_RH_HIERARCHY*)&(target->hierarchy), buffer, size);
+    if((result == TPM_RC_SUCCESS) && (target->tag == 0x8027))
+    {
+        TPMI_ALG_HASH digestVerified;
+        result = TPMI_ALG_HASH_Unmarshal(&digestVerified, buffer, size, FALSE);
+    }
     if(result == TPM_RC_SUCCESS)
         result =
             TPM2B_DIGEST_Unmarshal((TPM2B_DIGEST*)&(target->digest), buffer, size);
